# BUG: Lossy TLine Driver — FAIL 1.00e+00

## Circuit
`lossy_tline_driver.sp` — lossy transmission line driver, transient

## Symptom
FAIL with relative error 1.00e+00 (100%) vs ngspice.

## Root Cause (suspected)
100% relative error suggests BigOSpice output is near zero while ngspice produces nonzero values (or vice versa).
The LTRA (lossy transmission line) model may not be propagating signals correctly in transient simulation.
Possible: LTRA convolution history not initialized, or the lossy line stamp is wrong.

## Key Files
- `crates/device/src/ltra.rs` — LTRA model eval and history updates
- `crates/solver/src/stamper.rs` — LTRA special-path stamping (lines ~500-575)
- `crates/analysis/src/transient.rs` — `update_ltra_histories` call
